WEBVTT

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:11.378
William Tell by Friedrich von Schiller, Penguin Reader's Level 1, Scene 1, in Outdorf, Switzerland.

00:00:11.438 --> 00:00:16.192
This is an important day.

00:00:16.252 --> 00:00:19.344
We're going to meet with Governor Gessler.

00:00:19.404 --> 00:00:21.435
We can't be late.

00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:29.366
Our Austrian emperor and his governors don't understand the Swiss people.

00:00:29.426 --> 00:00:31.852
We aren't Austrians.

00:00:31.912 --> 00:00:33.553
We're Swiss.

00:00:33.613 --> 00:00:36.343
And we love our country.

00:00:36.403 --> 00:00:41.044
And we don't want to give our money to Austria.

00:00:41.104 --> 00:00:44.315
Here's one of Gessler's soldiers.

00:00:44.375 --> 00:00:45.965
It's time.

00:00:46.025 --> 00:00:48.666
Let's go in and talk.

00:00:48.726 --> 00:00:55.238
Gessler must understand our problems.

00:00:55.298 --> 00:00:59.968
What do you want now?

00:01:00.028 --> 00:01:07.463
You Swiss people come here every day with a new problem.

00:01:07.523 --> 00:01:10.466
Our problems aren't new.

00:01:10.526 --> 00:01:13.418
You never listen to us.

00:01:13.477 --> 00:01:17.911
Things are difficult in Switzerland these days.

00:01:17.971 --> 00:01:19.532
Difficult?

00:01:19.592 --> 00:01:21.874
I don't understand.

00:01:21.934 --> 00:01:26.058
Your soldiers are always watching us.

00:01:26.117 --> 00:01:30.946
Every day you put a new tax on us.

00:01:31.006 --> 00:01:38.275
There are taxes on our food, our houses and our animals.

00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:42.026
How can we live with these taxes?

00:01:42.086 --> 00:01:45.428
Perhaps you can't.

00:01:45.488 --> 00:01:49.320
But I can live very well with them.

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:52.702
And the Emperor is happy with them too.

00:01:52.762 --> 00:01:55.753
But we're very unhappy.

00:01:55.813 --> 00:01:58.904
We don't want to be Austrians.

00:01:58.964 --> 00:02:00.362
We're Swiss.

00:02:00.422 --> 00:02:02.661
Please listen to us.

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:07.664
Your Austrian emperor is very good to you.

00:02:07.724 --> 00:02:11.105
But you don't understand him.

00:02:11.165 --> 00:02:12.456
That's right.

00:02:12.516 --> 00:02:16.228
And he doesn't understand us.

00:02:16.288 --> 00:02:19.580
This is our country now.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:21.000
Go home.

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:24.813
Listen to me and to the emperor.

00:02:24.873 --> 00:02:33.707
Or things are going to get very dangerous for every Swiss man, woman and child.

00:02:33.767 --> 00:02:34.797
Go!

00:02:34.857 --> 00:02:37.418
I don't want to talk to you.

00:02:37.478 --> 00:02:45.010
My time is important, and you are not!

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:50.223
What did the Governor say?

00:02:50.283 --> 00:02:54.336
Is he going to send his soldiers back to Austria?

00:02:54.396 --> 00:02:58.530
Is he going to stop putting taxes on us?

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:02.312
Did he understand our problems?

00:03:02.372 --> 00:03:06.546
No, he didn't listen to us.

00:03:06.606 --> 00:03:09.618
What can we do?

00:03:09.678 --> 00:03:12.750
Can we stop this man?

00:03:12.810 --> 00:03:14.852
Perhaps we can.

00:03:14.912 --> 00:03:18.549
But first, we must find a hero.

00:03:18.609 --> 00:03:21.086
A Swiss hero.

00:03:21.146 --> 00:03:24.958
Yes.

00:03:25.017 --> 00:03:29.240
Scene two.

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:34.322
At a river in the Swiss mountains.

00:03:34.382 --> 00:03:38.424
I'm going home now.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:41.096
Look, it's going to rain.

00:03:41.156 --> 00:03:43.933
I must get my boat from the river.

00:03:43.993 --> 00:03:48.162
It's getting cold, and the water looks dangerous.

00:03:48.222 --> 00:03:49.724
Winter's coming.

00:03:49.784 --> 00:03:51.345
Good night, Rudy.

00:03:51.405 --> 00:03:52.116
Wait.

00:03:52.176 --> 00:03:53.026
Look.

00:03:53.086 --> 00:03:54.668
Who's coming?

00:03:54.728 --> 00:03:56.780
I know that, man.

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.752
It's Coraad Bongarden.

00:03:59.812 --> 00:04:02.244
Help me, my friends.

00:04:02.304 --> 00:04:04.376
Boatman, quick.

00:04:04.436 --> 00:04:07.018
Take me across the river now.

00:04:07.078 --> 00:04:09.120
Or I'm a dead man.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:10.281
Please.

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:11.934
What's the problem?

00:04:11.994 --> 00:04:13.688
Who wants to kill you?

00:04:13.748 --> 00:04:15.219
Guessler's men.

00:04:15.279 --> 00:04:16.510
They're coming.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:17.430
Quick!

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.632
Why are they looking for you?

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:23.294
I killed one of the governor's tax men.

00:04:23.354 --> 00:04:25.076
I was at work.

00:04:25.136 --> 00:04:26.906
Away from home.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:30.158
The man came to my house.

00:04:30.218 --> 00:04:33.430
He asked my wife for water.

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:36.372
And then he wanted hers.

00:04:36.432 --> 00:04:39.595
My wife came to me for help.

00:04:39.654 --> 00:04:41.976
I went home quickly.

00:04:42.036 --> 00:04:45.179
And then I killed him with my knife.

00:04:45.238 --> 00:04:47.321
You did well.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.732
Rudy, quick!

00:04:49.792 --> 00:04:52.995
Take him across the river in your boat.

00:04:53.055 --> 00:04:54.367
I can't!

00:04:54.426 --> 00:04:58.730
The river's moving very quickly and the rain is heavy.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:01.862
No boat can go across the river now.

00:05:01.922 --> 00:05:05.256
Rudy, you must help this man.

00:05:05.316 --> 00:05:07.277
He has a family.

00:05:07.337 --> 00:05:10.773
I have a wife and three sons too.

00:05:10.832 --> 00:05:12.316
Look at the river.

00:05:12.376 --> 00:05:13.927
It's dangerous.

00:05:13.987 --> 00:05:15.588
I want to help.

00:05:15.648 --> 00:05:17.230
But I can't.

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:18.990
And I'm dead.

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.143
A man is coming.

00:05:21.202 --> 00:05:24.044
Oh, it's William Tell.

00:05:24.104 --> 00:05:26.357
Good evening, my friends.

00:05:26.416 --> 00:05:27.928
What's wrong here?

00:05:27.988 --> 00:05:31.990
Bound Garden killed one of the governor's tax men.

00:05:32.050 --> 00:05:34.512
The soldiers are looking for him.

00:05:34.572 --> 00:05:38.135
But our boatman can't take him across the river.

00:05:38.195 --> 00:05:40.016
The river's dangerous.

00:05:40.076 --> 00:05:41.093
Look at it.

00:05:41.152 --> 00:05:44.049
But Baumgarden can't wait here.

00:05:44.109 --> 00:05:45.800
What can we do?

00:05:45.860 --> 00:05:49.252
There's my boat and there's the river.

00:05:49.311 --> 00:05:52.733
You can take the boat and be the hero.

00:05:52.793 --> 00:05:54.944
I'm going to stay here.

00:05:55.004 --> 00:05:57.896
Baumgarden, let's go quickly.

00:05:57.956 --> 00:06:06.369
Bernie, send my love to my family.

00:06:06.428 --> 00:06:15.902
Scene 3 at Stalfakha's home.

00:06:15.962 --> 00:06:19.683
Your story isn't new.

00:06:19.743 --> 00:06:29.726
The Emperor's governors, his Austrian soldiers, and his tax men make new problems for us every day.

00:06:29.786 --> 00:06:33.508
Gessler is playing games with our country.

00:06:33.568 --> 00:06:36.608
We don't want to kill people.

00:06:36.668 --> 00:06:38.759
We don't want to fight.

00:06:38.819 --> 00:06:41.019
We're men of peace.

00:06:41.079 --> 00:06:43.299
But what can we do?

00:06:43.359 --> 00:06:48.281
Let's find a number of good, strong Swiss men.

00:06:48.341 --> 00:06:51.222
We must stop these Austrians.

00:06:51.282 --> 00:06:55.174
I'm going to visit Walter first tomorrow.

00:06:55.234 --> 00:06:57.524
He loves our country.

00:06:57.584 --> 00:06:59.215
He can help us.

00:06:59.275 --> 00:07:01.956
We must fight for our country.

00:07:02.016 --> 00:07:03.667
Let's start now.

00:07:03.727 --> 00:07:06.798
Yes, we must help our country.

00:07:06.858 --> 00:07:09.878
But can't we find peace?

00:07:09.938 --> 00:07:11.828
I'm going home.

00:07:11.888 --> 00:07:14.069
My family are waiting.

00:07:14.129 --> 00:07:20.782
But remember, you can always ask for my help.

00:07:20.842 --> 00:07:24.415
Scene 4.

00:07:24.475 --> 00:07:29.048
In the mountains near Tell's home.

00:07:29.107 --> 00:07:32.615
Hello!

00:07:32.675 --> 00:07:35.872
You're the famous governor-guessler.

00:07:35.932 --> 00:07:37.023
Am I right?

00:07:37.083 --> 00:07:38.654
You're right.

00:07:38.714 --> 00:07:40.435
And who are you?

00:07:40.495 --> 00:07:42.666
My name's William Tell.

00:07:42.726 --> 00:07:45.428
I'm a hunter, and I'm Swiss.

00:07:45.488 --> 00:07:48.279
Oh, that's interesting.

00:07:48.339 --> 00:07:51.040
But I haven't got time for you.

00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:56.204
I'm an important man, with important work in outdoor.

00:07:56.263 --> 00:07:57.154
Move.

00:07:57.214 --> 00:07:58.424
Wait!

00:07:58.484 --> 00:08:00.826
First we must talk.

00:08:00.886 --> 00:08:02.756
Then you can go.

00:08:02.816 --> 00:08:06.248
Why do I want to talk to you?

00:08:06.308 --> 00:08:09.100
Because this is my country.

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:14.464
You're making problems for us with your taxes and your soldiers.

00:08:14.523 --> 00:08:18.536
The people of this country are very unhappy.

00:08:18.596 --> 00:08:21.749
Wait, will you tell?

00:08:21.809 --> 00:08:25.042
I know about you.

00:08:25.062 --> 00:08:27.173
You helped Baumgarten!

00:08:27.233 --> 00:08:31.294
Yes, but Baumgarten is a good man.

00:08:31.354 --> 00:08:36.023
He killed your tax man, because the man was dangerous.

00:08:36.082 --> 00:08:39.804
Aren't you a dangerous man too?

00:08:39.864 --> 00:08:43.636
Don't you always have a crossbow with you?

00:08:43.696 --> 00:08:48.287
Don't you go into the mountains every day and kill?

00:08:48.307 --> 00:08:50.598
I kill animals.

00:08:50.658 --> 00:08:53.939
I put food on my family's table.

00:08:53.999 --> 00:08:56.250
I don't kill people.

00:08:56.310 --> 00:08:58.781
Can your soldiers say that?

00:08:58.841 --> 00:09:01.596
I haven't got time for your talk.

00:09:01.656 --> 00:09:02.712
Move!

00:09:02.772 --> 00:09:03.762
Now!

00:09:03.822 --> 00:09:04.834
Why?

00:09:04.894 --> 00:09:06.524
It's not late.

00:09:06.584 --> 00:09:09.348
Please, listen to me.

00:09:09.408 --> 00:09:13.490
You and your taxes are bad for Switzerland.

00:09:13.550 --> 00:09:15.892
We don't want you here.

00:09:15.952 --> 00:09:18.955
But I am here.

00:09:19.015 --> 00:09:21.940
And I'm going to stay.

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:32.538
This is a new Switzerland and you must listen to us and you must understand the Swiss people.

00:09:32.598 --> 00:09:38.400
We love our country, our mountains and our families.

00:09:38.460 --> 00:09:43.772
We want peace and we're going to fight for it.

00:09:43.832 --> 00:09:48.256
Watch us.

00:09:48.316 --> 00:09:52.851
Scene five.

00:09:52.911 --> 00:09:56.063
At William Tell's home.

00:09:56.123 --> 00:10:00.376
You're going to have problems with Gessler now.

00:10:00.436 --> 00:10:01.466
Why?

00:10:01.526 --> 00:10:03.338
I talked to him.

00:10:03.398 --> 00:10:04.869
I didn't hit him.

00:10:04.929 --> 00:10:07.550
But he's going to remember you.

00:10:07.610 --> 00:10:10.312
He's going to make problems for us.

00:10:10.372 --> 00:10:11.774
Wait and see.

00:10:11.834 --> 00:10:14.094
I'm a man of peace.

00:10:14.154 --> 00:10:17.507
I'm going to stay away from Governor Gessler now.

00:10:17.567 --> 00:10:19.322
Please do that.

00:10:19.382 --> 00:10:21.888
Where are Valta and Wilhelm?

00:10:21.948 --> 00:10:23.368
They're in the garden.

00:10:23.428 --> 00:10:25.248
They're playing a game.

00:10:25.308 --> 00:10:26.598
Look at them.

00:10:26.658 --> 00:10:28.229
They're little soldiers.

00:10:28.289 --> 00:10:31.070
William, this isn't good.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:34.780
My sons aren't going to be soldiers.

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:39.592
I want peace in my country and in my family.

00:10:39.652 --> 00:10:42.094
I understand, Hedwig.

00:10:42.154 --> 00:10:45.387
Our sons are going to be hunters.

00:10:45.447 --> 00:10:50.140
But one day, our country is going to want soldiers too.

00:10:50.200 --> 00:10:56.255
At that time, every man, woman and child must fight for Switzerland.

00:10:56.315 --> 00:10:59.598
William, can't you go to the Emperor?

00:10:59.658 --> 00:11:03.620
Can't you and your friends talk to him about peace?

00:11:03.680 --> 00:11:05.452
Yes, we're going to try.

00:11:05.472 --> 00:11:07.684
But then...

00:11:07.744 --> 00:11:11.326
Father, are we going to Outdorf now?

00:11:11.386 --> 00:11:12.715
Yes, my son.

00:11:12.775 --> 00:11:14.414
Have you got your crossbow?

00:11:14.474 --> 00:11:16.954
Why is he taking his crossbow?

00:11:17.014 --> 00:11:18.475
I'm a hunter.

00:11:18.535 --> 00:11:23.077
I want to teach my son about the mountains and about hunting.

00:11:23.137 --> 00:11:24.698
He's a good student.

00:11:24.757 --> 00:11:28.219
But the mountains are dangerous for a young boy.

00:11:28.279 --> 00:11:30.320
We're mountain people.

00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:33.531
This country isn't dangerous for us.

00:11:33.591 --> 00:11:37.032
I'm going to watch Valter and teach him.

00:11:37.092 --> 00:11:39.903
And why are you going to Outdorf?

00:11:39.963 --> 00:11:42.040
We're going to visit your father.

00:11:42.100 --> 00:11:43.697
I want to talk to him.

00:11:43.757 --> 00:11:47.470
My father and his friends want to start a fight.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.512
Please don't go, William.

00:11:49.572 --> 00:11:51.343
You're a man of peace.

00:11:51.403 --> 00:11:52.424
I must go.

00:11:52.444 --> 00:11:55.366
I must help Switzerland, too.

00:11:55.426 --> 00:11:58.289
But guess there's an outdoor today.

00:11:58.349 --> 00:12:00.180
He doesn't like you.

00:12:00.240 --> 00:12:02.612
Stay at home and go tomorrow.

00:12:02.672 --> 00:12:03.464
No.

00:12:03.524 --> 00:12:05.374
I must go today.

00:12:05.434 --> 00:12:06.886
Let's go, Valter.

00:12:06.946 --> 00:12:08.688
Valter mustn't go.

00:12:08.748 --> 00:12:09.868
Please.

00:12:09.928 --> 00:12:11.779
He can stay with me.

00:12:11.839 --> 00:12:13.949
I want to go with father.

00:12:14.009 --> 00:12:16.871
I want to see the town and the people.

00:12:16.931 --> 00:12:23.174
Hedwig, he's going to be okay with me.

00:12:23.234 --> 00:12:30.308
Scene six in Alstof.

00:12:30.368 --> 00:12:38.498
Switzerland has an Austrian emperor and Austrian taxes.

00:12:38.558 --> 00:12:43.894
But the Swiss people are always a problem.

00:12:43.954 --> 00:12:49.804
What problems can I give them today?

00:12:49.864 --> 00:12:52.535
Give them a new tax.

00:12:52.595 --> 00:12:57.086
No, there was a new tax yesterday.

00:12:57.146 --> 00:13:01.447
You stopped games on Saturdays and Sundays too.

00:13:01.507 --> 00:13:04.176
And you closed the cafes.

00:13:04.236 --> 00:13:09.820
You can stop all music after six o'clock in the evening.

00:13:09.880 --> 00:13:13.445
Yes, very interesting.

00:13:13.504 --> 00:13:16.948
But I'm thinking, what?

00:13:17.008 --> 00:13:19.880
What can you do?

00:13:19.940 --> 00:13:25.622
There's a tall thin tree in front of my office.

00:13:25.682 --> 00:13:29.723
Bring me one of my old hats.

00:13:29.783 --> 00:13:34.284
Now put the hat on the tree.

00:13:34.344 --> 00:13:41.987
Then I want to talk to the people.

00:13:42.047 --> 00:13:47.969
People of Switzerland!

00:13:48.030 --> 00:13:54.272
You can see a hat on the tree in front of you.

00:13:54.332 --> 00:13:57.173
Why is it there?

00:13:57.233 --> 00:13:59.303
Can you think?

00:13:59.363 --> 00:14:01.014
We don't know.

00:14:01.034 --> 00:14:03.624
Is it important?

00:14:03.684 --> 00:14:07.626
It's very important to you.

00:14:07.686 --> 00:14:12.137
You all love me and your emperor.

00:14:12.197 --> 00:14:14.447
Is that right?

00:14:14.507 --> 00:14:16.826
What did she say?

00:14:16.886 --> 00:14:18.497
She's happy.

00:14:18.557 --> 00:14:19.757
That's all.

00:14:19.818 --> 00:14:27.000
You can't see me every day because I have a lot of important work.

00:14:27.060 --> 00:14:32.822
But you can stop every day and look at my hat.

00:14:32.882 --> 00:14:40.945
You can send your love to the Emperor and to me too.

00:14:41.005 --> 00:14:42.085
Our love.

00:14:42.145 --> 00:14:44.296
How can we love a hat?

00:14:44.356 --> 00:14:45.956
All the Austrians.

00:14:46.016 --> 00:14:49.127
Must we stop for your old hat?

00:14:49.187 --> 00:14:50.348
Yes!

00:14:50.408 --> 00:14:53.810
All of you must stop!

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:58.862
My soldiers are going to be here every day!

00:14:58.922 --> 00:15:05.874
They're going to watch you!

00:15:05.934 --> 00:15:10.346
Scene 7.

00:15:10.406 --> 00:15:15.359
In front of the tree with the hat.

00:15:15.419 --> 00:15:20.091
People aren't going to walk here.

00:15:20.151 --> 00:15:23.041
They don't want to stop for a hat.

00:15:23.101 --> 00:15:27.162
Perhaps they don't love the Emperor and his governor.

00:15:27.222 --> 00:15:29.733
But it's only a hat.

00:15:29.793 --> 00:15:32.394
It's not on the Emperor's head.

00:15:32.454 --> 00:15:36.425
I don't want to make problems for people.

00:15:36.485 --> 00:15:40.206
But this is our job.

00:15:40.266 --> 00:15:44.526
Look, a man and a boy are coming.

00:15:44.586 --> 00:15:46.704
Let's watch them.

00:15:46.764 --> 00:15:51.865
Father, does every country have tall, beautiful mountains?

00:15:51.925 --> 00:15:53.166
No, son.

00:15:53.226 --> 00:15:56.538
Switzerland is famous for its mountains.

00:15:56.598 --> 00:15:59.120
We Swiss understand them.

00:15:59.180 --> 00:16:01.422
And I'm going to teach you.

00:16:01.482 --> 00:16:05.954
Look, Father, why is there a hat on that tree?

00:16:06.014 --> 00:16:07.606
I don't know.

00:16:07.666 --> 00:16:09.878
But it's not important.

00:16:09.938 --> 00:16:11.088
Let's go.

00:16:11.148 --> 00:16:12.208
Stop!

00:16:12.268 --> 00:16:17.168
In the name of the Emperor of Austria, stop!

00:16:17.228 --> 00:16:20.166
And look up at the hat.

00:16:20.226 --> 00:16:21.146
No.

00:16:21.206 --> 00:16:22.327
Why?

00:16:22.387 --> 00:16:24.719
No questions.

00:16:24.778 --> 00:16:26.240
Come with us.

00:16:26.300 --> 00:16:28.090
What are you talking about?

00:16:28.150 --> 00:16:30.062
You're coming with us.

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:31.652
To prison.

00:16:31.712 --> 00:16:33.444
I don't understand.

00:16:33.504 --> 00:16:35.295
What's the problem here?

00:16:35.355 --> 00:16:36.806
Stop.

00:16:36.866 --> 00:16:39.287
This man is from my family.

00:16:39.347 --> 00:16:40.778
What's the problem?

00:16:40.838 --> 00:16:43.660
He didn't stop for the hat.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.161
He doesn't love the emperor.

00:16:46.222 --> 00:16:47.464
Friends.

00:16:47.524 --> 00:16:49.556
Look at this!

00:16:49.616 --> 00:16:55.020
Do we want a hat on a tree in our streets?

00:16:55.080 --> 00:16:57.821
Is this an emperor?

00:16:57.881 --> 00:17:01.734
You can't take William Tell away.

00:17:01.794 --> 00:17:04.235
He's a man of peace.

00:17:04.295 --> 00:17:06.166
Don't take Tell!

00:17:06.226 --> 00:17:09.998
The governor is coming!

00:17:10.059 --> 00:17:13.891
Is there a problem here?

00:17:13.951 --> 00:17:15.789
Yes, governor.

00:17:15.850 --> 00:17:21.068
This man and his son didn't stop for your hat.

00:17:21.128 --> 00:17:23.958
We're taking them to prison.

00:17:24.018 --> 00:17:29.559
But the people of the town are with him, not us.

00:17:29.620 --> 00:17:31.890
Is the hat important?

00:17:31.950 --> 00:17:34.050
I'm sorry, Governor.

00:17:34.110 --> 00:17:35.961
But there's no problem.

00:17:36.021 --> 00:17:43.070
This afternoon, tomorrow and every day I'm going to stop and look up at your hat.

00:17:43.130 --> 00:17:47.729
I want peace in Altdorf and in all of Switzerland.

00:17:47.789 --> 00:17:49.379
William, tell!

00:17:49.439 --> 00:17:55.500
You're a difficult man and you have your crossbow with you again.

00:17:55.560 --> 00:18:01.592
My father can hit an apple on a tree from a hundred feet with his crossbow.

00:18:01.652 --> 00:18:03.302
Can he?

00:18:03.362 --> 00:18:09.014
Soldier, bring me an apple.

00:18:09.074 --> 00:18:12.354
Good.

00:18:12.414 --> 00:18:13.654
Tell!

00:18:13.714 --> 00:18:21.260
Take your son to that tree across the street and put this apple on his head.

00:18:21.320 --> 00:18:25.182
Then take your crossbow and walk away.

00:18:25.202 --> 00:18:31.566
Hit the apple and you and your son can live.

00:18:31.626 --> 00:18:33.728
On my son's head.

00:18:33.788 --> 00:18:36.400
No father can do that.

00:18:36.461 --> 00:18:38.031
Kill me now.

00:18:38.091 --> 00:18:38.912
No!

00:18:38.972 --> 00:18:40.102
Do it!

00:18:40.163 --> 00:18:43.538
You and your crossbow are famous.

00:18:43.598 --> 00:18:50.376
Boy, stand near the tree and wait for your father's arrow.

00:18:50.436 --> 00:18:52.578
Governor, stop.

00:18:52.638 --> 00:18:58.852
Take my money and my house, but don't kill Tel and Volta.

00:18:58.913 --> 00:19:01.154
I'm going to be okay.

00:19:01.214 --> 00:19:03.526
Father can hit this apple.

00:19:03.586 --> 00:19:06.088
There's no problem.

00:19:06.148 --> 00:19:08.780
Tel, wait.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:13.332
Your hand is moving and your eyes are swimming in your head.

00:19:13.392 --> 00:19:17.251
Don't play this man's games, Governor.

00:19:17.311 --> 00:19:18.611
Kill me.

00:19:18.671 --> 00:19:20.362
Not my son.

00:19:20.422 --> 00:19:24.342
I want to watch you with your crossbow.

00:19:24.402 --> 00:19:25.533
Do it!

00:19:25.593 --> 00:19:28.164
Father, you can do it.

00:19:28.224 --> 00:19:29.964
I'm going to be okay.

00:19:30.024 --> 00:19:32.574
Yes, you can do it, tell.

00:19:32.634 --> 00:19:34.185
You're a hero.

00:19:34.245 --> 00:19:35.645
Tells our man.

00:19:35.705 --> 00:19:38.886
We don't want that hat on the tree.

00:19:38.946 --> 00:19:40.146
Tell.

00:19:40.206 --> 00:19:43.292
Hit the apple and go home.

00:19:43.352 --> 00:19:44.410
Look!

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:46.628
Your son is waiting!

00:19:46.688 --> 00:19:54.480
You can do it, Father!

00:19:54.540 --> 00:20:02.274
They did it!

00:20:02.334 --> 00:20:05.605
Look, Father, I'm okay.

00:20:05.665 --> 00:20:07.005
I'm not dead.

00:20:07.065 --> 00:20:14.297
Every Swiss man, woman and child is going to hear about William Tell.

00:20:14.357 --> 00:20:16.187
He's our hero.

00:20:16.247 --> 00:20:18.417
Tell could hit an apple.

00:20:18.477 --> 00:20:20.358
Or a soldier.

00:20:20.418 --> 00:20:24.018
Walter, William, let's go to my house.

00:20:24.078 --> 00:20:25.078
Come with me.

00:20:25.138 --> 00:20:26.219
Stop!

00:20:26.279 --> 00:20:28.839
I want to talk to Tell.

00:20:28.899 --> 00:20:30.480
Yes, Governor.

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:32.922
Good job, tell.

00:20:32.982 --> 00:20:38.436
But where's your second arrow in my shirt?

00:20:38.496 --> 00:20:42.990
Why did you have a second arrow?

00:20:43.050 --> 00:20:44.662
It was for you.

00:20:44.722 --> 00:20:47.924
A dead governor for a dead son.

00:20:47.984 --> 00:20:53.558
But now the arrow can stay in my shirt, and I can go home.

00:20:53.618 --> 00:20:54.890
Goodbye.

00:20:54.950 --> 00:20:57.072
An arrow for me!

00:20:57.092 --> 00:20:58.698
Soldiers!

00:20:58.758 --> 00:21:00.604
Take him to prison!

00:21:00.664 --> 00:21:04.276
He's not going to walk away from me!

00:21:04.336 --> 00:21:05.527
No!

00:21:05.587 --> 00:21:06.338
Wait!

00:21:06.398 --> 00:21:08.150
He's a good man!

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:10.101
He's a man of peace!

00:21:10.161 --> 00:21:12.003
He's our hero!

00:21:12.063 --> 00:21:16.446
You're a very bad man, Governor Gessler.

00:21:16.506 --> 00:21:22.292
I'm not going to kill you, Tel, but you're dangerous.

00:21:22.352 --> 00:21:26.600
I'm going to put you in prison, in Kuznacht.

00:21:26.660 --> 00:21:30.995
I don't want you and your crossbow on these streets.

00:21:31.055 --> 00:21:38.766
Soldiers, take him to my boat.

00:21:38.826 --> 00:21:49.668
Scene eight on the governor's boat.

00:21:49.728 --> 00:21:56.033
Why is tell important to the governor?

00:21:56.093 --> 00:21:59.258
He's very good with the crossbow.

00:21:59.318 --> 00:22:03.340
And he's a hero to the Swiss people.

00:22:03.400 --> 00:22:05.911
The governor doesn't like it.

00:22:05.971 --> 00:22:10.362
But the Swiss people love him now.

00:22:10.422 --> 00:22:13.964
Look at this rain.

00:22:14.024 --> 00:22:17.386
It's very dangerous on the water.

00:22:17.446 --> 00:22:20.406
Where's our hero now?

00:22:20.466 --> 00:22:24.090
We're never going to arrive at Kuzna.

00:22:24.150 --> 00:22:26.444
Where's my boatman?

00:22:26.504 --> 00:22:28.294
Here I am, Governor.

00:22:28.354 --> 00:22:29.995
What's wrong?

00:22:30.055 --> 00:22:32.626
When are we going to arrive?

00:22:32.686 --> 00:22:35.197
The rain's very heavy, Governor.

00:22:35.257 --> 00:22:37.598
And the water's dangerous.

00:22:37.658 --> 00:22:40.349
I'm not a strong man.

00:22:40.409 --> 00:22:43.470
I'm having problems with the boats.

00:22:43.530 --> 00:22:46.341
Soldiers, help the boatman.

00:22:46.401 --> 00:22:49.092
What do they know about boats?

00:22:49.152 --> 00:22:50.443
Get some help.

00:22:50.503 --> 00:22:51.478
Now!

00:22:51.538 --> 00:22:55.326
The prisoner tells good with boats.

00:22:55.386 --> 00:23:00.519
Bring the prisoner to me.

00:23:00.579 --> 00:23:04.102
Tell!

00:23:04.162 --> 00:23:06.192
Help us with this boat!

00:23:06.252 --> 00:23:07.994
How can I help you?

00:23:08.054 --> 00:23:09.324
Look at me.

00:23:09.384 --> 00:23:12.246
I'm a prisoner, not a boatman.

00:23:12.306 --> 00:23:15.378
You're not a prisoner now, tell.

00:23:15.438 --> 00:23:22.608
Boatman, here's your helper!

00:23:22.668 --> 00:23:27.968
Here we are!

00:23:28.028 --> 00:23:31.769
Soldiers, take town to the prison.

00:23:31.829 --> 00:23:32.899
What?

00:23:32.959 --> 00:23:34.260
Prison?

00:23:34.320 --> 00:23:39.162
No, I'm going to take my crossbow and say goodbye.

00:23:39.222 --> 00:23:41.502
Where did he go?

00:23:41.562 --> 00:23:46.744
He helped us, and now he's going to help his people.

00:23:46.804 --> 00:23:49.234
He is a hero.

00:23:49.294 --> 00:23:50.686
Stop him!

00:23:50.746 --> 00:23:52.368
An out of door!

00:23:52.428 --> 00:23:54.630
He wanted to kill me!

00:23:54.690 --> 00:23:56.871
But we can't see him!

00:23:56.931 --> 00:24:01.994
But I can see you!

00:24:02.054 --> 00:24:03.766
Oh no!

00:24:03.826 --> 00:24:05.847
The governor's dead!

00:24:05.907 --> 00:24:07.618
Where's Tell?

00:24:07.678 --> 00:24:10.160
He's in the mountains now.

00:24:10.220 --> 00:24:12.562
We can never find him.

00:24:12.622 --> 00:24:20.790
Let's take our dead governor to his house in Kuznak.

00:24:20.850 --> 00:24:28.708
Scene 9, in a street in Outstorf.

00:24:28.768 --> 00:24:30.868
William!

00:24:30.928 --> 00:24:32.609
You're back!

00:24:32.669 --> 00:24:36.450
How did you get away from Gessler and his soldiers?

00:24:36.510 --> 00:24:39.962
I helped them with their boat on a very bad night.

00:24:40.022 --> 00:24:42.622
Then I killed the governor.

00:24:42.683 --> 00:24:44.173
Yes!

00:24:44.233 --> 00:24:48.774
Now things are going to be good again in our country.

00:24:48.834 --> 00:24:53.457
Gessler's dead, but we must finish Tell's work.

00:24:53.517 --> 00:24:57.530
We must send the Austrians back to their home.

00:24:57.590 --> 00:25:00.182
Let's start our fight today.

00:25:00.242 --> 00:25:03.554
Tell your our hero.

00:25:03.614 --> 00:25:05.435
Can you help us again?

00:25:05.495 --> 00:25:07.125
Of course I can.

00:25:07.186 --> 00:25:11.548
Every Swiss person is going to fight for their country.

00:25:11.608 --> 00:25:19.580
Many years from now, our children's children are going to talk about our fight.

00:25:19.640 --> 00:25:23.008
He's Gessler's hat!

00:25:23.068 --> 00:25:25.260
What can we do with that?

00:25:25.320 --> 00:25:26.981
Do we want it?

00:25:27.041 --> 00:25:28.792
Put it in the river!

00:25:28.852 --> 00:25:31.114
Send it to Austria!

00:25:31.174 --> 00:25:32.216
Wait!

00:25:32.276 --> 00:25:35.548
Let's put it in an important place.

00:25:35.608 --> 00:25:39.991
Let's look at it every day and remember Gessler.

00:25:40.051 --> 00:25:42.593
Let's say, never again!

00:25:42.653 --> 00:25:44.794
Switzerland is for the Swiss!

00:25:44.854 --> 00:25:47.356
Yeah!

00:25:47.416 --> 00:25:50.926
But isn't the emperor going to look for you?

00:25:50.986 --> 00:25:54.206
Isn't he going to come here with his soldiers?

00:25:54.266 --> 00:25:55.246
Yes.

00:25:55.307 --> 00:25:59.470
Gessler was his friend and one of his governors.

00:25:59.529 --> 00:26:01.792
But we are strong.

00:26:01.852 --> 00:26:04.423
And we can stop the soldiers.

00:26:04.484 --> 00:26:07.696
We can wait for them in the mountains.

00:26:07.756 --> 00:26:10.319
We must listen to William Tell.

00:26:10.379 --> 00:26:11.300
You're right.

00:26:11.360 --> 00:26:12.590
But wait.

00:26:12.650 --> 00:26:14.142
Who's coming?

00:26:14.202 --> 00:26:16.104
It's Staufacher.

00:26:16.164 --> 00:26:17.564
Listen!

00:26:17.624 --> 00:26:20.772
The Emperor is dead!

00:26:20.832 --> 00:26:21.968
What?

00:26:22.028 --> 00:26:23.009
How?

00:26:23.069 --> 00:26:23.979
When?

00:26:24.039 --> 00:26:29.311
Many Austrian people didn't like Gessler or the Emperor.

00:26:29.371 --> 00:26:34.172
The Emperor was on the road to Baden here in Switzerland.

00:26:34.232 --> 00:26:38.404
Some Austrians stopped him and killed him.

00:26:38.464 --> 00:26:41.445
Then they went back to Austria.

00:26:41.505 --> 00:26:45.016
This is a good day for our country.

00:26:45.076 --> 00:26:48.504
Now we've got an important job.

00:26:48.564 --> 00:26:52.094
We must build a strong Switzerland.

00:26:52.154 --> 00:26:54.756
We can have peace now.

00:26:54.817 --> 00:26:57.008
Goodbye, my friends.

00:26:57.068 --> 00:27:02.432
I'm going home to the mountains and to my family.

00:27:02.492 --> 00:27:04.244
Thank you, William.

00:27:04.304 --> 00:27:08.387
Switzerland is always going to remember you.

00:27:08.447 --> 00:27:10.559
You're our hero!

00:27:10.619 --> 00:27:11.269
Yes!

00:27:11.329 --> 00:27:13.291
William Tell!

